# CLAUDE.md (placeholder)

AI agent instructions for the **dev edition** of Ascendo live in
`dev-sync-overlay/ai-instructions/CLAUDE.md` and are pushed to a
private Proton overlay via `dev-sync-export.sh`.

Public contributors don't need this file. The repo is configured so
that `claude` (or any other AI coding assistant) doesn't need it to
work — it picks up project conventions from `CONTRIBUTING.md`,
`README.md`, and the per-package `pyproject.toml` files.

If you're a maintainer setting up a fresh dev machine: run
`dev-sync-import.sh` to restore the real `CLAUDE.md` alongside the
rest of the dev-edition overlay.

See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for project conventions.
